      <h2>Coverage in Rural Areas and National Parks</h2>
      <p>Dialog has the best rural 4G coverage, but even Dialog has dead zones. Areas where signal is consistently weak or absent: deep inside Sinharaja Rainforest, certain sections of the Knuckles Range, and remote parts of Wilpattu National Park. In Yala, Udawalawe and Minneriya you typically get 3G–4G signal on Dialog near the entrances but it drops on game drives. The Hill Country is better than you'd expect — major towns like Ella, Nuwara Eliya and Haputale have good 4G coverage. Train journeys through mountain tunnels will lose signal temporarily. Download offline Google Maps for the Cultural Triangle, Hill Country and national parks before you leave a town with strong WiFi.</p>

      <h2>eSIM Options for Sri Lanka</h2>
      <p>If you have a compatible phone (most iPhone XS and later, and many modern Android flagships support eSIM), a travel eSIM lets you activate data before you fly — so you have Google Maps and messaging working from the moment you land, without queueing at the airport SIM counter. Travel eSIMs are particularly useful if you're <strong>visiting multiple countries</strong> on one trip (Sri Lanka plus Maldives or India, for example), since a single eSIM plan covers all of them without swapping physical SIMs.</p>

